import SwiftUI
struct PreprocessInformationView:View {
    var body:some View {
        VStack(alignment:.leading,spacing:9) {
            LessonRichText(text:"**One grid, separate populations**\nChoose column rules once. Training is required for learned preprocessing; Validation and Test are optional. Each output retains its own row identities and partition role.")
            LessonRichText(text:"**Training-only learning**\nMissing-value replacements, categorical vocabularies and population standard deviations are learned from retained Training rows. The same captured rules prepare all connected partitions; held-out values never update them. Learned rules are retained with the run and model export without another canvas node.")
            LessonRichText(text:"**Table cleanup order**\nNormalize Unicode → remove selected characters → whitespace → case → empty-to-missing → missing policy. Rules refer to original named columns; retained rows keep their IDs. No type casts or statistics are learned. NFC composes canonical equivalents; NFKC also folds compatibility forms.\n\n**Exact text behavior**\nRemove controls deletes Unicode Cc characters, including tabs and newlines. Remove punctuation deletes all P categories; decimal digits means Nd, including non-ASCII decimal digits. Trim uses Unicode whitespace at both ends. Collapse replaces Unicode whitespace runs with one ASCII space and trims ends. Lowercase and Uppercase use Unicode mappings, independent of machine locale; they may change text length. Empty is distinct from null until Convert to missing is selected.\n\n**Partitioned preparation order**\nExclude rows first, replace missing cells, encode categories, then scale numeric columns. Keep preserves a missing value; it does not make scaling or encoding accept one. Table cleanup supports Preserve, Stop run, Drop row and typed fixed values without fitting. Formula coalesce supports custom replacements; Filter can route missing rows.")
            LessonRichText(text:"**Boundaries**\nText controls require Text columns. Numeric and Boolean fixed values must match the inherited type. Images and temporal values support Preserve, Drop row and Stop run, with no fixed literals. Unconfigured columns pass through. One-hot categories replace their source column; unknown categories either stop or produce an all-zero block with a diagnostic. Constant numeric columns use scale 1. Configuration changes need Apply; source/run evidence is never silently refreshed.")
        }
    }
}
